<Base canonicalPath="/about-us/" title="About Ula" description="The idea behind Ula: a considered, independent guide to discovering Tamil Nadu at your own pace.">
<PageHeading label="VANAKKAM. THIS IS ULA." title="Go a little closer." description="To the places. To their stories. To the small moments that make a journey stay with you."/><div class="about-landscape"><Photo src="/images/mamallapuram.webp" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"/><span>Stone, sea and a little time. Mamallapuram.</span></div><section class="about-statement wrap"><span class="meta">THE IDEA</span><div><h2>Tamil Nadu deserves<br/>more than a checklist.</h2><p>Ula brings together temple towns, hill landscapes and coastal places in a guide that gives you room to explore. We start with a few destinations and thoughtful routes, then leave the pace to you.</p><p>A local breakfast can be as memorable as a landmark. A quiet street can change how you remember a city. This is a place to begin noticing both.</p><a class="text-link" href="/destinations/">Find your first destination</a></div></section><Culture/><section class="planning-notes wrap"><h2>Made as a travel<br/>design concept.</h2><div><p>Ula is an independent personal portfolio project. The destinations are real; the itineraries are editorial suggestions. It offers a browser-based trip brief rather than bookings.</p><a class="text-link" href="/colophon/">Sources and photography credits</a><a class="text-link" href="/privacy/">Your saved trip and privacy</a></div></section>
</Base>
